# Implementation Plan - Step 2: Real-time WebSocket Communication

Add real-time WebSocket communication between the Vanilla JS frontend and FastAPI backend for VoxVision AI.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **WebSocket Endpoint**: The server will expose a WebSocket route at `ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws/chat`.
> **Connection Strategy**: The frontend will establish a persistent WebSocket connection with automatic exponential-backoff reconnection logic if the server disconnects.
> **Design Integrity**: All visual additions will preserve the existing human-designed dark interface without adding excessive animations or neon effects.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Python + FastAPI)

#### [NEW] [backend/app/api/websocket.py](file:///c:/Users/LEGION/GIT/vox-vision-ai/backend/app/api/websocket.py)
- Implement `ConnectionManager` class to track active WebSocket clients and handle message broadcasting/unicasting.
- Define WebSocket endpoint `/ws/chat`:
  - Receives JSON payload: `{"type": "chat_message", "message": "user input", "session_id": "default"}`
  - Responds with JSON payload: `{"type": "chat_response", "reply": "VoxVision AI (WebSocket): ...", "status": "success", "timestamp": "..."}`
  - Supports heartbeat ping/pong: `{"type": "ping"}` -> `{"type": "pong", "timestamp": "..."}`

#### [MODIFY] [backend/app/main.py](file:///c:/Users/LEGION/GIT/vox-vision-ai/backend/app/main.py)
- Register `websocket_router` from `app.api.websocket`.

